+| HTML pipeline compatibility | Several tests used React merely to reach save, compactness, action mapping, layout, or observability behavior, coupling unrelated assertions to unsupported framework components. | Those behavioral operands use HTML. Their save/tag, action mapping, layout, compact render, latency, and error-observability assertions remain; `Heading` was replaced by the supported `Text` where a framework-neutral schema was needed. | `packages/mcp-server/test/contracts/contract-alignment.spec.ts`; `packages/mcp-server/test/contracts/error-observability.contract.spec.ts`; `packages/mcp-server/test/contracts/layout-single-source.spec.ts`; `packages/mcp-server/test/e2e/action-mappings.e2e.spec.ts`; `packages/mcp-server/test/tools/pipeline.compact.spec.ts` |
+| Adapter/basic bridge parity | Adapter parity accepted the basic mix but did not reject fictional imports or require normalized props. | The supported basic mix remains successful over JSON-RPC and asserts real React/Vue imports, shared CSS, and normalized `content` props. | `packages/mcp-adapter/test-s57-m05.js` |
+| Historical adapter guard | `s57-m01` expected its React style-syntax guard and unrelated catalog-size threshold to pass. | The `code.generate` guard remains green. The script remains 3/4 because the independent catalog assertion observes 48,257 characters against its 25,000 limit; this is unchanged at pre-M04 `96f1fbe` and catalog scope was not altered. | `packages/mcp-adapter/test-s57-m01.js` |
+| Legacy smoke/reproduction utilities | Utility scripts can call the bridge with historical operands, but are not M04 acceptance carriers. | Recorded as audited, not silently promoted into evidence and not rewritten as production/source refactors. | `packages/mcp-adapter/opus-4.6-repro.js`; `tools/agents-smoke/src/ux-flow-smoke.ts` |
